// Agent Scheduler benchmark suite.
//
// SYNTHETIC ONLY. Every population is generated by
// agent_scheduler::SyntheticLaboratory from an explicit seed and describes LOGICAL
// profiles (agents, capabilities, work requirements), not physically present hardware
// or remote nodes. Every measurement below is a single-process, in-memory measurement
// of this library. No multi-node or multi-GPU claim is implied, measured, or made, and
// no physical scale is claimed from a synthetic population.
//
// NO TIMEOUTS. There is no CTest TIMEOUT, no shell timeout wrapper, and no watchdog
// process anywhere in this suite. Benchmarks run to completion naturally. A correctness
// guard failure is reported by exit code 1 after the run finishes, never by killing it.
//
// Every reported row counts COMPLETED operations (not enqueues, not requests), prints
// the iteration count actually executed, and reports elapsed milliseconds and ops/sec
// with a fixed two-decimal format. Correctness guards assert the logical outcome of
// every phase (assignment counts agree with the decisions that reported them,
// candidates examined match agents x work items, invariants are clean) and fail loudly.
//
// Apache License 2.0. Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs. No telemetry transmission.

